<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1">
  <DUT Name="E_DeviceConnectionStatus" Id="{8a1d6c39-4e72-4b05-8f13-7a9c0e4b1d62}">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[(*
    Purpose:
        Combined device diagnostic verdict for a single common EtherCAT slave.
        It reduces the two verdicts FB_DeviceDiagnostics derives from the slave
        PDO inputs - LinkStatus (E_EcCommState) and DataStatus (E_DataStatus) -
        into one value a consumer can act on with a single comparison.

    Usage:
        Declare it as the type of a diagnostic status member, typically the
        pytmc-exposed ConnectionStatus output/property of an I_DeviceDiagnostics
        implementation (FB_DeviceDiagnostics is the reference one):

            eConnectionStatus : E_DeviceConnectionStatus;
            IF eConnectionStatus <> E_DeviceConnectionStatus.Connected THEN
                // slave unhealthy: NotOperational, WcError or Stale
            END_IF

        Members:
            Connected       LinkStatus = OP and DataStatus = Ok
            NotOperational  LinkStatus <> OP
            WcError         LinkStatus = OP, DataStatus = WcError
            Stale           LinkStatus = OP, DataStatus = Stale

        LinkStatus gates DataStatus: while the slave is not in OP the value is
        NotOperational whatever the data quality, because WcState and
        InputToggle carry no meaning before the state machine reaches OP.
        Consumers read this value instead of re-deriving the verdict, so a
        change of the mapping rules happens in one place.

        The encoding is implicit (Connected = 0 ... Stale = 3, UDINT) and is
        published to EPICS as io: i, so it is part of the interface: append new
        members at the end and never renumber or reorder existing ones.

    Objectives:
        - Give every EtherCAT slave one stable, self-describing verdict instead
          of each consumer recombining three raw PDO inputs differently.
        - Keep "not connected" (NotOperational) separate from "connected but
          unusable data" (WcError, Stale), so the two failure modes can be
          alarmed on and diagnosed independently.
        - Preserve a numeric encoding that stays stable for EPICS/archiver
          consumers and for the diagnostic statuses built on it.

    History:
        2026-08-20  Mandza <ysmandza@slac.stanford.edu>: created together with
                    I_DeviceDiagnostics/I_BridgeDiagnostics and their
                    implementations (commit 94833bd).
        2026-11-27  taio: header expanded to state purpose, usage, objectives
                    and history as the POU/DUT header convention requires
                    (audit finding 1073). No member, value or encoding changed.

    Author/Date: Mandza <ysmandza@slac.stanford.edu>, 2026-08-20.
*)
TYPE E_DeviceConnectionStatus :
(
    Connected,       // LinkStatus = OP and DataStatus = Ok
    NotOperational,  // LinkStatus <> OP
    WcError,         // LinkStatus = OP, DataStatus = WcError
    Stale            // LinkStatus = OP, DataStatus = Stale
) UDINT;
END_TYPE]]></Declaration>
  </DUT>
</TcPlcObject>
